# Ownership split: anyone can open PRs anywhere, but merges into
# platform-owned paths require platform-team review. App manifests
# (apps/*/base, apps/*/env, apps/*/chart) are deliberately NOT listed —
# app teams own their deployment config.
#
# `personalize.sh` rewrites the org part of the slug below for you. Two things
# it cannot decide for you:
#   - Only *organization* forks can use a `@org/team` owner. If you forked into
#     a personal account, replace each owner with your plain `@username` —
#     GitHub silently ignores code owners it cannot resolve, so an unedited
#     slug here means these paths end up with no required review at all.
#   - `platform-team` is a placeholder team name; swap in your real one.

/bootstrap/          @yhxlele/platform-team
/kargo-shared/       @yhxlele/platform-team
/apps/*/argocd/      @yhxlele/platform-team
/apps/*/kargo/       @yhxlele/platform-team
/.github/            @yhxlele/platform-team
/docs/               @yhxlele/platform-team
